  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Here Power is constant,<br />Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>v</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>v</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>v</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>v</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/></math></p><p>Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"/>Simplifying further we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;its clear that the graph won&#39;t be straight line so first &amp; third options cant be correct.<br />Now, from equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;its clear that when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is increased then the slope&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;should also increase which is possible in second option. Hence option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;is correct.&nbsp;</p>"
  }
